{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-5477-r4535144","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Beef and Barley Stew","sourcePageId":5477,"sourceRevision":"4535144","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2025-09-01T23:39:58Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Beef%20and%20Barley%20Stew&oldid=4535144","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T12:24:42.134Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Easy recipes","Category:Inexpensive recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes for stew","Category:Recipes using barley","Category:Recipes using beef","Category:Recipes using beef broth and stock","Category:Recipes using carrot","Category:Recipes using celery","Category:Recipes using garlic","Category:Recipes using green bean","Category:Recipes using marjoram","Category:Recipes using vegetable oil","Category:Recipes using wheat flour","Category:Recipes with metric units"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"e69e196726222a43f7532dd88e9598ee0a423a278e39d573dcc423835abc0589","sourceWikitext":"__NOTOC__\n{{recipesummary|category=Stew recipes|servings=12|time=2 hours|difficulty=2}}\n\n{{recipe}} | [[Cookbook:Cuisine of the United States|United States]] | [[Cookbook:Meat Recipes|Meat]] | [[Cookbook:Stews|Stews]]\n\n'''Beef and barley stew''' is a hearty [[Cookbook:Stew|stew]] that can be prepared from freezer to table in under 2 hours. It's easy to prepare ahead of time and refrigerate or freeze for later use.\n\n==Ingredients==\n*3 pounds (1.25 kg) [[Cookbook:Beef|beef]], cubed\n*1 white [[Cookbook:Onion|onion]], diced\n*4 cubed [[Cookbook:Potato|potatoes]]\n*1 cup (240 g) [[Cookbook:Barley|barley]]\n*¼ cup (60 g) [[Cookbook:Flour|flour]]\n*1 can [[Cookbook:Tomato Paste|tomato paste]]\n*1 small can [[Cookbook:Dice|diced]] [[Cookbook:Tomato|tomatoes]]\n*1 slug [[Cookbook:Worcestershire Sauce|Worcestershire sauce]]\n*1 bunch [[Cookbook:Parsley|parsley]]\n*[[Cookbook:Salt|salt]], [[Cookbook:Pepper|pepper]], [[Cookbook:Paprika|paprika]] to taste\n*1 teaspoon [[Cookbook:Thyme|thyme]]\n*2 teaspoons [[Cookbook:Marjoram|marjoram]]\n*2 tablespoons [[Cookbook:Vegetable oil|vegetable oil]]\n*2 cartons [[Cookbook:Broth|beef broth]]\n*1 lb (450 g) [[Cookbook:Mushroom|mushrooms]]\n*1 pkg [[Cookbook:Green Bean|frozen green beans]]\n*3 cloves halved [[Cookbook:Garlic|garlic]]\n*3 stalks [[Cookbook:Celery|celery]]\n*4 large [[Cookbook:Carrot|carrots]]\n*water, enough to cover all ingredients in pot\n\n== Procedure ==\n\n=== Variation I ===\n\n# Dust beef cubes lightly with flour, then brown in vegetable oil.\n# Move to separate pot and clean pan with beef broth and add to pot.\n# Sauté celery, garlic and onion briefly and add to pot. Simmer for 1.5 hours.\n# Add barley and simmer additional ½ hour.\n# Add potatoes, sliced mushrooms, frozen green beans, diced tomatoes and tomato paste. \n# Add slug of Worcestershire sauce. Simmer for 1 additional hour.\n# Chop parsley and stir into stew before serving.\n\n=== Variation II ===\n#Combine the flour, salt, pepper, and paprika on a plate, and dredge the cubed beef in the flour mixture.\n#Add the oil to a [[Cookbook:Dutch Oven|Dutch oven]] or large [[Cookbook:Saucepan|saucepan]] on medium high heat.  [[Cookbook:Browning|Brown]] the beef in the oil.\n#When the beef is evenly browned on all sides, add the water, beef broth, bay leaf, onion, carrots and barley.  Allow to come to a simmer and reduce heat.\n#Allow to simmer for 1 to 1½ hours, until the meat is tender.  Remove the bay leaf and serve with noodles or rice.\n\n==Notes, tips, and variations==\n*Don't overcrowd the beef when browning. If there is not enough room to brown all the meat at the same time, do it in batches, and then add the reserved beef with the other ingredients.\n\n==Warnings==\n*Always follow safe handling guidelines when using raw meat.\n\n[[Category:Recipes for stew]]\n[[Category:Recipes using beef]]\n[[Category:Inexpensive recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes_with_metric_units]]\n[[Category:Recipes using barley]]\n[[Category:Recipes using carrot]]\n[[Category:Recipes using celery]]\n[[Category:Recipes using wheat flour]]\n[[Category:Recipes using garlic]]\n[[Category:Recipes using beef broth and stock]]\n[[Category:Recipes using vegetable oil]]\n[[Category:Recipes using marjoram]]\n[[Category:Recipes using green bean]]","isRecipe":false,"recipe":{"name":"Beef and Barley Stew","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"3 pounds (1.25 kg) beef, cubed","sourceText":"3 pounds (1.25 kg) beef, cubed","amountText":"3 pounds (1.25 kg) beef, cubed","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"1 white onion, diced","sourceText":"1 white onion, diced","amountText":"1 white onion, diced","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"4 cubed potatoes","sourceText":"4 cubed potatoes","amountText":"4 cubed potatoes","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-4","name":"1 cup (240 g) barley","sourceText":"1 cup (240 g) barley","amountText":"1 cup (240 g) barley","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-5","name":"¼ cup (60 g) flour","sourceText":"¼ cup (60 g) flour","amountText":"¼ cup (60 g) flour","amount":null,"unit":